  'curtains.faq.1.q': 'How much do glass curtains cost per square metre?',
  'curtains.faq.1.a': 'Glass curtains in Alicante typically cost between \u20AC250 and \u20AC450 per square metre, depending on the height, glass thickness (8 mm or 10 mm) and the number of panels. We offer a free quote including a home visit.',
  'curtains.faq.2.q': 'Do glass curtains insulate against the cold?',
  'curtains.faq.2.a': 'Glass curtains provide significant protection against wind and cold, although they are not airtight like a fixed window. In Alicante, where winters are mild, they are usually enough to enjoy the terrace all year round with a noticeable temperature difference compared to the outside.',
  'curtains.faq.3.q': 'Can glass curtains close completely?',
  'curtains.faq.3.a': 'Yes, the panels close fully with minimal gaps between them. However, they are not completely airtight like a fixed enclosure. This allows some natural ventilation, which helps prevent condensation.',
  'curtains.faq.4.q': 'What glass thickness is used in glass curtains?',
  'curtains.faq.4.a': 'We use 8 mm or 10 mm safety tempered glass, depending on the dimensions and wind exposure. Tempered glass is up to 5 times stronger than standard glass and, if broken, shatters into small pieces without sharp edges.',
  'curtains.faq.5.q': 'Do glass curtains steam up?',
  'curtains.faq.5.a': 'Condensation can occur on cold, humid days, especially if there is a temperature difference between inside and outside. A proper installation with an adjustable ventilation system minimises this effect. In the Alicante climate, condensation is infrequent.',
  'curtains.faq.6.q': 'Can glass curtains be installed on a pergola?',
  'curtains.faq.6.a': 'Yes, this is one of the most popular combinations. Glass curtains complement a bioclimatic pergola perfectly, creating an enclosed, sheltered outdoor space that can be enjoyed 365 days a year.',
  'curtains.faq.7.q': 'Do they survive Costa Blanca levante storms?',
  'curtains.faq.7.a': 'Yes. Properly installed with reinforced rails and 10 mm tempered glass, they withstand gusts over 100 km/h. As an extra precaution we recommend partially opening panels during strong storms to reduce pressure on the fixings.',
  'curtains.faq.8.q': 'Can they be installed on a rental terrace?',
  'curtains.faq.8.a': "Yes, though you need the owner's consent and, where applicable, the community's authorisation. They're a demountable element: at the end of the tenancy they can be removed leaving only the rails behind. Some owners accept them as a permanent property improvement.",
